    "kind": "definition_of_done",
    "summary": "- Tokens are 32 `crypto/rand` bytes in unpadded base64url (43 chars). Only the SHA-256 hash is stored. The token appears only in the invite email; POST and GET `/v1/invites` and snapshots never carry it.\n- `/v1/invites/accept` returns 404 `invite_not_found` (unknown or revoked), 410 `invite_used` (already accepted), or 410 `invite_expired` (older than 7 days on the service clock). Otherwise it accepts as before.\n- Re-inviting an address (case-insensitive) revokes the older open invite, so only the newest token works. GET lists only pending invites, each with `expires_at`. Checked by new store \n...[truncated]",
